# Kaggle API credentials.
#
# ONLY needed for the optional fourth dataset (Customer Support on Twitter).
# The three core datasets are public HTTP and need no account at all.
#
#   1. python3 scripts/download_data.py --init-env   # copies this file to .env
#   2. Sign in or sign up at https://www.kaggle.com
#   3. Go to https://www.kaggle.com/settings
#   4. Under "API", click "Create New Token" -- a kaggle.json file downloads.
#      Open it in any text editor; it holds your username and key:
#        {"username":"janedoe","key":"a1b2c3d4e5f6..."}
#   5. Paste both values into .env (this file is only the template).
#   6. python3 scripts/download_data.py --all
#
# .env is gitignored, so your key cannot be committed by accident.
# Never put real credentials in this file -- .env.example IS committed.

KAGGLE_USERNAME=
KAGGLE_KEY=
